  "body": "Further to discussion in #5087 ([specifically starting from this point in the thread](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5087#issuecomment-612599624)), the following suggestions were made to improve clarity of the section about focusable areas, and the sequential focus order. The first two have been addressed in this PR. The latter requires a PR in the WHATWG web site repo, which I’d like to make before this one gets merged, if it sounds good to you.\n\n1. Add \"and be sequentially focusable\" before the list of elements that it is suggested browsers include in the \"tab\" order by default (i.e. when their tabindex value is null). (This is an editorial change because it clarifies the intention and behaviour that already exists.)\n2. Add a solid line to the top of the [focusable areas examples table](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#data-model), to match the one at the end, and make it clearer to see that the example panels are part of the table.\n\nAnother change discussed in #5087 was to remove [the special case for when there's only one example within a table cell](https://github.com/whatwg/whatwg.org/blob/fdc3a634888c3cb48f33637c3f26e232c3b655ee/resources.whatwg.org/standard.css#L300-L306) from the [focusable areas example table](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#data-model), in order to make the layout more consistent and easier to parse (given that this table has an unusual layout). However, that special case is used in two other tables: [the sections usage summary table](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#usage-summary-2) and the [text-level semantics usage summary table](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#usage-summary). Given the discussion we’ve already had, I’m expecting to remove the special case only for the focusable areas table. It seems the cleanest way of doing this would be to make a PR that changes standard.css in the WHATWG web site repo—which I’ll do if that sounds good to you?\n\nThis will close #5087—but, if at all possible, I’d like to make the separate style change PR first.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/2ecceea...dd2a17d/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">/browsers.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/2ecceea...dd2a17d/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/2ecceea...dd2a17d/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/2ecceea...dd2a17d/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 10, 2020, 3:24 PM UTC (dd2a17d)\">/common-dom-interfaces.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5506/2ecceea...dd2a17d/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated o